\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Probability density functions of the \emph  {continuous} recovery laws corresponding to the three regimes in BehaviorSpace experiments\nobreakspace  {}\texttt  {05}--\texttt  {07} (same \texttt  {recovery-mean}, \texttt  {power-law-lambda}, and \texttt  {lognormal-sigma} as in \path {netlogo/behaviorspace_experiments.xml}). All three satisfy $\mathbb  {E}[W]=5$; the variances (legend) differ, with the heavy-tailed laws spreading mass toward longer infectious periods. The exponential curve is the continuous-time Markovian reference with rate $1/\mathbb  {E}[W]$ (the implementation samples a continuous draw and rounds to ticks, as in \path {netlogo/virus_simulation.nlogox}).}}{7}{figure.18}}
\newlabel{fig:recovery-pdfs}{{2}{7}{Probability density functions of the \emph {continuous} recovery laws corresponding to the three regimes in BehaviorSpace experiments~\texttt {05}--\texttt {07} (same \texttt {recovery-mean}, \texttt {power-law-lambda}, and \texttt {lognormal-sigma} as in \protect \path {netlogo/behaviorspace_experiments.xml}). All three satisfy $\mathbb {E}[W]=5$; the variances (legend) differ, with the heavy-tailed laws spreading mass toward longer infectious periods. The exponential curve is the continuous-time Markovian reference with rate $1/\mathbb {E}[W]$ (the implementation samples a continuous draw and rounds to ticks, as in \protect \path {netlogo/virus_simulation.nlogox})}{figure.18}{}}
